R = RECORD("K1", 1, "K2", 2, "K3", 3, "K4", 4, "K5", 5, "K6", 6, "K7", 7, "K8", 8, "K9", 9, "K10", 10, "K11", 11, "K12", 12, "K13", 13, "K14", 14, "K15", 15, "K16", 16, "K17", 17); R["Z"] = 5; S = RECORD("K1", 1, "K2", 2, "K3", 3, "K4", 4, "K5", 5, "K6", 6, "K7", 7, "K8", 8, "K9", 9, "K10", 10, "K11", 11, "K12", 12, "K13", 13, "K14", 14, "K15", 15, "K16", 16, "K17", 17); COUNT(S) & "/" & S["K17"]
--- expect
text "17/17"
===

### name: record.shape.width-17-missing-key-is-e-no-key
--- note
Reading the added key from a fresh record is the ordinary E_NO_KEY, never a host
array-index failure.
--- source
R = RECORD("K1", 1, "K2", 2, "K3", 3, "K4", 4, "K5", 5, "K6", 6, "K7", 7, "K8", 8, "K9", 9, "K10", 10, "K11", 11, "K12", 12, "K13", 13, "K14", 14, "K15", 15, "K16", 16, "K17", 17); R["Z"] = 5; S = RECORD("K1", 1, "K2", 2, "K3", 3, "K4", 4, "K5", 5, "K6", 6, "K7", 7, "K8", 8, "K9", 9, "K10", 10, "K11", 11, "K12", 12, "K13", 13, "K14", 14, "K15", 15, "K16", 16, "K17", 17); S["Z"]
--- expect
error E_NO_KEY at 1:376
===

### name: record.shape.width-20-assigned-key-does-not-leak
--- note
A 20-field record gains a key; a record built afterwards from the same 20 keys
has exactly those keys and not the added one. Lisp's shape table was corrupted
from 16 fields (LISP-C2). Cases run in one process, so a shape poisoned here is
seen by the cases below.
--- source
R = RECORD("K1", 1, "K2", 2, "K3", 3, "K4", 4, "K5", 5, "K6", 6, "K7", 7, "K8", 8, "K9", 9, "K10", 10, "K11", 11, "K12", 12, "K13", 13, "K14", 14, "K15", 15, "K16", 16, "K17", 17, "K18", 18, "K19", 19, "K20", 20); R["Z"] = 5; S = RECORD("K1", 1, "K2", 2, "K3", 3, "K4", 4, "K5", 5, "K6", 6, "K7", 7, "K8", 8, "K9", 9, "K10", 10, "K11", 11, "K12", 12, "K13", 13, "K14", 14, "K15", 15, "K16", 16, "K17", 17, "K18", 18, "K19", 19, "K20", 20); HAS(S, "Z")
--- expect
bool FALSE
===

### name: record.shape.width-20-count-and-read
--- note
The same records read back: count 20, the last field present, and the key the
first record gained absent (E_NO_KEY at the index).
--- source
R = RECORD("K1", 1, "K2", 2, "K3", 3, "K4", 4, "K5", 5, "K6", 6, "K7", 7, "K8", 8, "K9", 9, "K10", 10, "K11", 11, "K12", 12, "K13", 13, "K14", 14, "K15", 15, "K16", 16, "K17", 17, "K18", 18, "K19", 19, "K20", 20); R["Z"] = 5; S = RECORD("K1", 1, "K2", 2, "K3", 3, "K4", 4, "K5", 5, "K6", 6, "K7", 7, "K8", 8, "K9", 9, "K10", 10, "K11", 11, "K12", 12, "K13", 13, "K14", 14, "K15", 15, "K16", 16, "K17", 17, "K18", 18, "K19", 19, "K20", 20); COUNT(S) & "/" & S["K20"]
--- expect
text "20/20"
===

### name: record.shape.width-20-missing-key-is-e-no-key
--- note
Reading the added key from a fresh record is the ordinary E_NO_KEY, never a host
array-index failure.
