### name: alias.assign-copy-then-write-through-an-alias-read
--- note
A copy of a value is independent (§3.4), but a read of `A` inside the index of a write to `A` is a live alias: the write happens in place and the pending read must see it. A host that implements copies lazily (copy-on-write with path copying) breaks exactly this: the write relocates A's root and the pending read holds the old one, which has no key "k". Regression guard against any such optimisation.
--- source
X = 1; A = X; A[A["k"]="k"]
--- expect
text "k"
===
